  'Pisces_H10': `With the North Node in Pisces, the call is toward a public role guided by compassion and vision, while the South Node in Virgo keeps perfecting the details of the job. The tenth house is career, reputation, and the public role, so here the growth is toward a public life guided by vision and compassion rather than rigid control.

Lives with this placement are here to grow toward a calling with soul in it ... toward work that serves and inspires, a public path followed on faith rather than micromanaged, and a reputation built on compassion instead of flawless technical control. The pull is real but unfamiliar, because the reflex is to perfect every detail, criticize every result, and treat the career as a problem to be endlessly corrected. It's not just learning to trust the path; it's structural identity expressed through a public self that grows by surrendering to a larger vision. Turned shadow, it's the placement that retreats into the Virgo comfort of the perfectly controlled career, that polishes the work to paralysis and avoids the riskier work of a public life led by faith and compassion.

The pull toward a soulful public path was always the growth. Following a vision on faith rather than perfecting it to death is the direction this life keeps being asked to grow.`,

  'Pisces_H11': `The North Node in Pisces asks for friendships and causes held with compassion, and the South Node in Virgo clings to critiquing the group from its edges. The eleventh house is friendship, community, and the wider circle, so here the growth is toward belonging held with compassion rather than judgment.

Lives with this placement are here to grow toward a circle bound by compassion ... toward friendships free of constant critique, causes embraced with idealism and faith, and a community joined in shared dreaming rather than in fixing everyone's flaws. The pull is real but unfamiliar, because the reflex is to evaluate the group, correct its members, and hold the whole circle to an exacting standard. This isn't learning to accept the group so much as a community life that grows through compassion, working at the level of identity, not habit. The trouble is the placement that retreats into the Virgo comfort of the critical, fault finding circle, that audits its friends and causes and avoids the riskier work of a community embraced with open hearted faith.

What was a circle held under scrutiny becomes, in time, a community bound by compassion and shared dreaming.`,

  'Pisces_H12': `In Pisces, the North Node calls toward surrender, compassion, and faith, while the South Node in Virgo keeps the old need to control and fix everything. The twelfth house is the unconscious, the unspoken, the mystical, and the dissolving of the self into something vast, and this is Pisces's own ground, the house it naturally rules. No placement asks the growth more directly than this one, because the call to surrender lands in the very realm of the boundless and the transcendent where the lesson lives.

Lives with this placement are here to grow toward the deepest letting go ... toward spiritual surrender, boundless compassion, trust in a current far larger than the self, and peace in the mystery that no amount of analysis can solve. The pull is real but unfamiliar, because the deepest reflex is to control, to worry, to pick the inner life apart in search of a flaw to fix. Learning to surrender is the easy read. The structural one is a hidden self that grows by dissolving its grip entirely. The shadow is the placement that retreats, unseen, into the Virgo comfort of an unconscious need to control and correct, that runs on buried anxiety and avoids the inner work of trusting what it cannot manage or understand.

An inner life long ruled by hidden control grows, in time, into a deep and unfamiliar surrender to the vast.`,

